{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5CwWLH84S8azpUrLgk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `addMonths` in `dates.js`. I could not run anything to check it, because Bash was denied in this session, so the verification below is by reading the code.\n\n**The bug:** `setMonth` doesn't clamp. For Jan 31 + 1 month it asked for \"Feb 31\", which rolls over to March 3. Customers billed on the 31st were therefore moved into the wrong month.\n\n**The fix:** the function now sets the day to 1 before changing the month, so nothing can overflow. It then clamps the day to the last day of the target month. The time of day is kept and the input date is not mutated, as before.\n\nI traced these by hand against the new code:\n- Jan 31, 2026 + 1 → Feb 28, 2026\n- Jan 31, 2024 + 1 → Feb 29, 2024 (leap year)\n- Mar 31, 2026 − 1 → Feb 28, 2026\n- Jan 15, 2026 + 1 → Feb 15, 2026 (unchanged from before)\n\nNothing has been run. Please run the existing date tests, or add a case for Jan 31 + 1 expecting Feb 28, before relying on this. If you want, I can add that test as well."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":745,"cache_read_input_tokens":23862,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":745},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb5b02ce-3a31-4280-ad3f-5e5b57a8232a","uuid":"2415c220-ac59-45bc-8461-b286ee00d6c6","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:30:14.348Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5CwMAacsigCyUJmWtK"}
